---
import ToolLayout from '@/layouts/ToolLayout.astro'
import RedactPdf from '@/components/tools/redact/docs/RedactPdf.tsx'
---

<ToolLayout slug="redact-pdf" width="wide">
  <RedactPdf client:load />

  <Fragment slot="explainer">
    <h2>How to redact a PDF</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Drop a PDF. The tool reads the text layer of each page and marks what it finds: emails, phone numbers, card and bank numbers, ID numbers, birth dates, addresses and keys.</li>
      <li>Load the language model to also find names, organizations and places.</li>
      <li>Check the Found list. Uncheck a value, or press its box on the page, to keep it.</li>
      <li>Drag on a page to add a box by hand, for example over a signature or a photo. Use Find a word to box every match of a word.</li>
      <li>Press Redact and download the file. The tool then reads the new file and tells you if a hidden value is still in it.</li>
    </ol>

    <h2>Why a black rectangle is not enough</h2>
    <p>
      A box drawn in a PDF editor sits on top of the text. The text is still in the file. Anyone can select the area and
      copy it, or open the file in another program and read it. Court filings and government documents have leaked
      this way many times.
    </p>

    <h2>What the PDF redactor does to the file</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>The tool renders each page that has a box to an image, paints the boxes into the pixels and replaces the page with the image. The text, fonts and drawings of that page are not copied.</li>
      <li>Redacted pages lose their selectable text. They cannot be searched or read aloud by a screen reader.</li>
      <li>Pages without a box are copied with their selectable text. Comments and other annotations are removed.</li>
      <li>Document properties (title, author, subject, keywords), XMP metadata, bookmarks, form data, attachments and scripts are removed from the whole file.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Choosing a resolution</h2>
    <p>
      150 DPI is good for reading on screen. Use 200 DPI for printing and 300 DPI for an archive. The resolution changes
      the file size and the sharpness of redacted pages. It does not change how well the text is removed.
    </p>

    <h2>What runs on your device</h2>
    <p>
      The PDF engine, the pattern rules and the optional language model all run in your browser. The model is a 19 MB
      file and its runtime is 14 MB; both download once from this site and then work offline.
    </p>

    <h2>How to check that nothing is uploaded</h2>
    <p>Open the Network tab in your browser's developer tools before you drop the file. No request carries the document.</p>

    <h2>Limits</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Only text in the text layer is found. A scanned page has no text layer: draw boxes by hand, or use the scanned document redactor, which reads pages with OCR.</li>
      <li>Text inside images, logos and signatures is not found. Box it by hand.</li>
      <li>Keep your original. Redaction cannot be undone.</li>
    </ul>
  </Fragment>
</ToolLayout>
